---
// About me, built from the Figma frames "About me" (1680), "About me / 1280", "About me / 1024" and "About me / Mobile 320".
// The hero is real text on a CSS gradient with fixed colours in both themes, as on the leadership page.
// From 760 the portrait sits on the bottom right and the text runs beside it; on phones the portrait
// stacks under the text. Wherever the text is smaller than large text, the light spot sits behind the portrait.
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Link from '../components/Link.astro';
import { footerLinks } from '../data/navigation';
import { url } from '../utils/url';
import '../styles/case-study.css';
import portrait from '../assets/about/portrait.png';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About me"
  description="Isabella Minzly, design leader in UI architecture, operational accessibility and design systems: how I got here, how I work and what I bring to global teams."
>
  <article class="case-study">
    <div class="about-hero">
      <div class="about-hero__text">
        <h1 class="about-hero__title">I build systems rather than isolated solutions.</h1>
        <div class="about-hero__body">
          <p>
            I am a design leader specialising in scalable UI architecture, operational accessibility and enterprise design capability across complex product
            ecosystems.
          </p>
          <p>
            I build patterns, frameworks and processes that work across products, teams and platforms, reduce friction for engineering, and place accessibility
            directly inside the delivery workflow.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Picture
        class="about-hero__portrait"
        src={portrait}
        alt="Portrait of Isabella Minzly, smiling, in a dark blazer and white shirt."
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
        widths={[277, 554, 770]}
        sizes="(width < 47.5em) 160px, 277px"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="what">
      <h2 id="what">What I do</h2>
      <h3>UI architecture</h3>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          At HCLSoftware I lead UI design for BigFix, where I own how the products in the BigFix family are structured, governed and implemented, from the first grid
          to the last chart. I lead a distributed team of designers there, and the Leadership page tells that story in full.
        </p>
        <div><Link href={url('/leadership/')}>Read more on the Leadership page</Link></div>
      </div>
      <h3>Accessibility as a capability</h3>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          I treat accessibility as an operational capability and not as a compliance exercise. I designed and delivered a structured programme that combines
          education, applied implementation and continuous improvement, built to WCAG 2.2 Level AA as a baseline and aligned with the European Accessibility Act and
          Section 508. More than 700 professionals across design, engineering, QA and product have completed it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <h3>Design systems, AI and governance</h3>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          I established design system and UI governance frameworks that standardise interaction patterns and speed up delivery. That work has taken shape as Mandala,
          an accessibility-first, token-driven design system that I am building at HCLSoftware, with AI and agentic approaches used thoughtfully and with intention.
          Knowledge and experience lead, and AI augments that work without replacing it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="here">
      <h2 id="here">How I got here</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          I began my career in the travel industry, where I worked as a product manager for many years, before going back to school to study design. I completed a
          Master's degree in design and spent the next years at a design bureau, where I designed and coded the front end of two websites for the Bank of Italy, built
          to the strictest level of accessibility. That project taught me early that a design is only as good as the way it is built, and it started a career-long
          interest in accessibility.
        </p>
        <p>
          I then freelanced for several years, working directly with clients, mostly in the fitness industry. There I designed an app for personalised training and
          live classes, built a video library, and created brand identities for training studios. Two of those projects are now case studies on this site.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2021 I joined HCLSoftware as a Senior Designer in the UX Center of Excellence. In 2022 I started My HCLSoftware and Marketplace from a blank screen, and
          the design language built there became the foundation of the BigFix interface from 2024, and then of Mandala.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="learner">
      <h2 id="learner">A curious, lifelong learner</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          I have never stopped learning. I completed the d.MBA in 2024, one of the most important courses I have taken, and I am constantly studying: taking courses,
          reading articles, attending conferences and webinars, and joining discussions with other people in the field.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="feedback">
      <span class="feedback__mark text-quote-mark-s" aria-hidden="true">“</span>
      <figure class="feedback__text">
        <blockquote class="text-quote_s">
          <p>
            Isabella really impressed me during her time at d.MBA. She stands out for her work ethic and her ability to think through problems from every angle.
            She’s detailed, strategic, and always focused on the 'why' behind the work.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption class="text-quote-attribution">Alen Faljic, Founder d.MBA & AI Makers Club</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="work">
      <h2 id="work">How I work</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          I combine strategic systems thinking with hands-on design leadership. I define standards, set the design direction, and work closely with engineering and
          product leadership, so that what reaches development is something people can build well.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work natively in Italian, English and Danish, and I have led design work across countries and time zones, which is a real advantage for global teams.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="beyond">
      <h2 id="beyond">Beyond the screen</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          My ideas rarely begin at a screen. They come from the rainforests, volcanoes and lakes I have travelled to, from Kandinsky and Leonardo da Vinci, from Bruce
          Lee's habit of inventing new rules instead of playing by his opponents', and from Vivaldi's Four Seasons in the background while I work. I tell more of that
          story on the Inspiration page.
        </p>
        <div><Link href={url('/about/inspiration/')}>Read more on the Inspiration page</Link></div>
        <p>
          I also speak about accessibility at conferences and events, and I teach it the way I learned to care about it, by starting with the person.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="hello">
      <h2 id="hello">Talk to me about ideas, collaboration or a coffee.</h2>
      <div><Button href={footerLinks.linkedIn}>Get in touch<span class="visually-hidden"> on LinkedIn</span></Button></div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Figma "Hero quote" on About me: white text on a light spot of accent, accent_default (light mode) at the edges.
     The colours stay the same in dark mode, because white on the dark-mode accent would fail.
     The paragraphs are smaller than large text, so the light spot sits behind the portrait and the text
     stays on 4.5:1 or more. */
  .about-hero {
    --hero-light: #7c88d7;
    --hero-edge: #5363ca;
    --portrait-width: 160px;

    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space_16);
    padding: var(--space_32) var(--space_16) 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 75% 30% at 50% 100%, var(--hero-light), var(--hero-edge));
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .about-hero__text,
  .about-hero__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space_10);
  }

  .about-hero__body {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-hero__title {
    font-family: var(--font-instrument-serif);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    line-height: 2.25rem;
  }

  .about-hero__portrait {
    display: block;
    inline-size: var(--portrait-width);
    block-size: auto;
  }

  /* From 760: portrait on the bottom right, text beside it */
  @media (width >= 47.5em) {
    .about-hero {
      /* The portrait scales with the hero (cqi is the width of main, which the hero fills); the text sets the height */
      --portrait-width: min(277px, 22cqi);

      position: relative;
      align-items: flex-start;
      /* The portrait is positioned on its own, so no gap is left for it */
      gap: 0;
      /* Never shorter than the portrait with 32 above it */
      min-block-size: calc(var(--portrait-width) * 475 / 385 + var(--space_32));
      padding: var(--space_32) var(--space_64) var(--space_32) var(--space_32);
      background: radial-gradient(ellipse 18% 60% at 90% 100%, var(--hero-light), var(--hero-edge));
    }

    .about-hero__text {
      /* The text may run into the right padding, which the portrait covers */
      inline-size: calc(100% + var(--space_64) - var(--portrait-width) - var(--space_24));
      max-inline-size: 49.5rem; /* 792 */
    }

    .about-hero__body {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      line-height: 2rem;
    }

    .about-hero__title {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      line-height: 3.5rem;
    }

    .about-hero__portrait {
      position: absolute;
      inset-block-end: 0;
      inset-inline-end: 0;
    }
  }

  /* 1680 layout: 400 high, as in the frame */
  @container main (width >= 77rem) {
    .about-hero {
      min-block-size: 25rem;
    }

    .about-hero__text {
      gap: var(--space_2);
    }

    .about-hero__body {
      gap: var(--space_16);
      line-height: 2.5rem;
    }

    .about-hero__title {
      font-size: 3.125rem; /* 50 */
      line-height: 6.875rem; /* 110 */
    }
  }

  /* Figma "Section: Quote": the same feedback quote as on Accessibility for Inclusion */
  .feedback {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space_16);
  }

  .feedback__mark {
    flex: none;
    color: var(--accent_default);
  }

  .feedback__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space_8);
    max-inline-size: 45.625rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
